%N A400261 The most significant digit of n' [the arithmetic derivative of n, A003415] in the primorial base, A049345.
%H A400261 Antti Karttunen, <a href="/A400261/b400261.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..10000</a>
%H A400261 <a href="/index/Pri#primorialbase">Index entries for sequences related to primorial base</a>.
%F A400261 a(n) = A276153(A003415(n)).
%F A400261 a(n) = A071178(A327859(n)).
%F A400261 a(n) = A067029(A400153(n)).
%F A400261 a(0) = a(1) = 0, and for n > 1, a(n) = A400260(n, A400262(n)-1).
%o A400261 (PARI) A400261(n) = if(n<=1, 0, my(f=factor(n), ad = n*sum(i=1, #f~, f[i, 2]/f[i, 1]), p=2, d=0); while(ad, d = ad%p; ad \= p; p = nextprime(1+p)); (d));
